{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Landed as Gerrit change 2363 -> origin/main commit e340337445e5 (LLM-Review+1 PASS, Verified+1, auto-submitted). \n\nFinal dispositions (all three ACs met):\n- AC#1 CODE ROOT via config.repo_root_or_none() (behavior-changing on a relocated store, each RED->GREEN in tests/unit/test_relocated_store_repo_root.py): reads.py sync.pull/tickets.branch/scratch.base_dir, freshness._remote_ref, fsck_tracker_health _branch_mismatch fallback/_tracker_sync_status/_configured_remote_ref.\n- AC#2 STORE ROOT via the ONE shared seam rebar._proc.store_repo_root(tracker) (== dirname(realpath(tracker)), marker '# repo-root-seam:', behavior-preserving): _proc.detached_child_cwd, compact_txn/compact_rebuild authorship-ledger, compact_plan attribution_fields, fsck.py repo_guess. sync.py:305/307 left as-is (already '# repo-root-ok:').\n- AC#3 guard scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py now unwraps str()/realpath()/abspath() and dirname(StorePaths(tracker).canonical) (feisty's blind spot); exempts only the seam + sanctioned sites. Self-test inverted realpath/abspath case + added .canonical/str/seam/single-seam cases.\n\nDISPOSITION CORRECTION (deviation from the operator's literal enumeration, consistent with principle #1): the plan-review gate (BLOCK, 2nd run) caught that freshness._remote_ref and fsck_tracker_health's three health-probe sites READ compose_config (via tickets.branch/tickets.remote), so by the compose_config discriminator they are CODE root, NOT store root as the operator shorthand 'fsck_*=store root' suggested. The principle governs bucketing, not the illustrative enumeration.\n\nCI-driven follow-up (patchset 2): converting the config-reads to repo_root_or_none() left 3 now-unused 'tracker' params (fsck_tracker_health._configured_remote_ref, reads._load_scratch, freshness._remote_ref) that tripped the ARG-backlog ratchet (tests/unit/.../test_arg_sweep_kwargs_heldout.py, 28>25). Removed the dead params + updated call sites and oracle calls. Verified+1 green on patchset 2.\n\nAttribution: caused-by c0f6-0fc9-fe48-41bc (injurious-pugnacious-azurevase, the config-root class origin). NOTE: the operator cited '594b-3118' for the class origin, but that ticket is 'Config-driven description cap' (unrelated); the verified config-root/injurious lineage is c0f6.\n\nfeisty-intense-mandrill folded: linked duplicates -> flowered, closed --class=duplicate --caused-by c0f6."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787974416838889001,"uuid":"692aea35-a575-46fb-9782-640f5cd0cd64"}